"""Replace the legacy soft-clustering section and add a clearly unrun YOLO plan."""
from pathlib import Path
import base64,json,re,html
import pandas as pd
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPORT=HERE.parent/'report_en_standalone.html'
def table(df):return '<div class=tw>'+df.to_html(index=False,border=0,float_format=lambda x:f'{x:.3f}')+'</div>'
def main():
    s=REPORT.read_text();a=json.loads((HERE/'audit.json').read_text());q=pd.read_csv(HERE/'summary.csv');b=a['selected'];k=int(b['k']);cov=b['covariance'];seed=int(b['seed'])
    main=q[q.dim.eq(32)].copy()
    t=main[['k','covariance','train_BIC_mean','val_loglik_mean','val_pmax_lt06_mean','val_mean_entropy_mean','seed_ARI','seed_entropy_rank_rho','val_organ_error_AUC_mean']]
    t.columns=['K','covariance','train BIC (mean)','val log density','val fraction pmax<0.6','val H/log(K)','seed ARI','entropy seed rho','organ-error AUC (mean)']
    dim=q[q.k.eq(20)&q.covariance.eq('diag')][['dim','val_mean_entropy_mean','val_pmax_lt06_mean','seed_ARI']].copy()
    dim.columns=['PCA dimensions','val H/log(K)','val fraction pmax<0.6','seed ARI']
    cases=pd.read_csv(HERE/'ambiguous_validation_cases.csv').head(8)
    ct=cases[['image_id','organ_category','pmax','p2','mean_seed_entropy','sd_seed_entropy','top1_component_organ','top2_component_organ']].copy()
    ct.columns=['image ID','canonical organ','p1','p2','mean seed H/log(K)','seed SD','top1 component dominant organ','top2 component dominant organ']
    ci=a['val_organ_error_AUC_CI95'];midci=a['val_midrange_AUC_CI95'];probe=a['organ_reference_probe']
    row=main[main.k.eq(k)&main.covariance.eq(cov)].iloc[0]
    png='data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((HERE/'soft_diagnostics.png').read_bytes()).decode()
    section='''<section id=e4><h2>4. Soft clustering: audit and train-only rerun</h2>
<div><span class='b v'>Rerun and checked</span> <span class='b e'>Model-conditional uncertainty</span> <span class='b x'>Multi-organ ground truth unavailable</span></div>
<dl><dt>What was wrong with the earlier interpretation?</dt><dd>
<p><b>The error target was species, not organ.</b> The old script reads <code>all_predictions.csv</code>, whose fields are <code>predicted_species</code>, <code>ground_truth_species</code> and <code>correct</code>. Thus its approximately 0.51 AUROC concerned species-classification error; it did not establish that entropy cannot flag organ-classification errors.</p>
<p><b>The fit used every image.</b> PCA and GMM were fit on all 1,641 images, including test images. That is a descriptive corpus fit, not an inductive held-out evaluation of uncertainty. BIC swept K but the illustrated memberships still used fixed K=20. A single diagonal-covariance choice and one arbitrary pmax threshold do not establish the amount of real biological overlap.</p>
<p><b>GMM probability is component allocation, not simultaneous organ presence.</b> The responsibilities sum to one across mutually exclusive mixture components. A near-one maximum may occur even for a poorly fitted or low-density image; it is not calibrated confidence that an organ is present. The posterior formula itself is valid. The issue is the protocol and what was inferred from it.</p></dd>
<dt>What was rerun?</dt><dd><p>EfficientNet only, using the checked-in raw embeddings. PCA is fit on the 1,181 training images and frozen; 249 individual-plant-disjoint validation images are assigned without refitting. No new test evaluation. Main sweep: unwhitened PCA-32, K=5/10/15/20/30/50, diagonal / tied / full covariance, five seeds, three EM initializations per seed, covariance regularization 1e-6 and maximum 300 iterations. All 138 fits in the main and dimension-sensitivity sweeps converged without recorded convergence warnings.</p>
<p>Entropy is normalized as H/log(K); pmax thresholds 0.6, 0.8 and 0.9, effective component counts and small component support are saved. Error bars are SD across optimization seeds, not confidence intervals over plants. BIC and held-out log density are compared only within a fixed PCA dimension and transformation. Separate 8-D / 16-D sensitivity runs use three seeds.</p></dd>
<dt>Results across K and covariance</dt><dd>'''+table(t)+f"<img src='{png}' alt='Train-only soft clustering: covariance and K sensitivity, validation density and uncertainty'>"+'''
<p><b>More certain can be worse.</b> At K=50, full covariance has almost hard allocations (mean fraction pmax&lt;0.6 = 0.002), yet mean validation log density collapses to −320.363, compared with 36.720 for diagonal and 36.714 for tied covariance in the same 32-D space. Full covariance at K=5 instead achieves 39.933. Many small full-covariance components overfit this training sample. High pmax alone is therefore not evidence of a good clustering, low error, or absence of mixed organs.</p>
<details><summary>Dimension sensitivity: diagonal covariance, K=20</summary>'''+table(dim)+'''<p>The ambiguous fraction changes from 9.4% at 8-D to 4.7% at 32-D under train-only fits. Reducing dimensions changes the modeled information; it is not a way to tune probabilities until they look soft. Do not compare BIC/log-density values across these different PCA spaces.</p></details>
</dd><dt>One frozen density model, chosen without validation tuning</dt><dd>'''+f'''
<p>Minimum training BIC among converged fixed-32-D candidates selects <b>K={k}, {html.escape(cov)} covariance, seed {seed}</b>. Its training BIC is {b['train_BIC']:,.1f}; mean validation log density {b['val_loglik']:.3f}. On validation, {b['val_pmax_lt06']:.1%} have pmax&lt;0.6, {b['val_pmax_lt08']:.1%} pmax&lt;0.8, and {b['val_pmax_lt09']:.1%} pmax&lt;0.9. Mean normalized entropy is {b['val_mean_entropy']:.3f}. This selects a density approximation, not a biological number of organs.</p>
<p>For this K/covariance across seeds: mean label ARI {row['seed_ARI']:.3f}, entropy-rank rho {row['seed_entropy_rank_rho']:.3f}, and top-25 entropy-set Jaccard {row['seed_top25_entropy_Jaccard']:.3f}. The ambiguous-image list is only moderately stable, even though most individual posterior allocations are near-hard.</p>
<p>A fixed train-only organ reference probe (balanced logistic regression, C=10, raw embeddings) has validation macro-F1 {probe['val_macroF1']:.3f}, with {probe['n_val_wrong']} errors among {probe['n_val']} known-organ images. The selected GMM entropy's AUROC for <b>these organ errors</b> is {b['val_organ_error_AUC']:.3f}, with individual-plant bootstrap 95% interval {ci[0]:.3f}–{ci[1]:.3f}. The old 0.51 used a different classifier target and fit protocol, so this is not a measured improvement over it.</p>
<p>Entropy versus provisional mid-range scale: AUROC {b['val_midrange_AUC']:.3f}, bootstrap interval {midci[0]:.3f}–{midci[1]:.3f}; the interval includes 0.5. Bootstrap intervals use 500 resamples of whole validation plants and are conditional on the fitted probe and selected GMM; they do not include model-selection or training uncertainty. These are diagnostics of uncalibrated scores.</p>
'''+'''</dd><dt>Ambiguous validation examples</dt><dd><p>Ranked by mean normalized entropy across the five seeds of the selected K/covariance. Detailed p1/p2 refer to the training-BIC selected seed. Component dominant organs are inferred from responsibility-weighted <b>training</b> label counts; they are descriptions of components, not predicted simultaneous organ labels.</p>'''+table(ct)+'''
</dd><dt>What this supports</dt><dd><p>The earlier “almost hard” observation persists under several fits, but its biological interpretation was too strong. Uncertainty depends on K, covariance and retained dimensions, and a badly fitting model can still look certain. Use held-out density, error association and seed stability together. To assess genuine multi-organ overlap, obtain independently annotated instance/multi-label organ ground truth. The existing 180-row <code>multi_label_audit.csv</code> is an <b>unfilled template</b>: all visible-organ, ambiguity and acceptable-label fields are blank, so it cannot validate overlap.</p>
<p class=note>The old all-corpus PCA32/diag20 setting was also rerun under installed scikit-learn 1.8.0 / float64: 1.46% pmax&lt;0.6, mean seed ARI 0.630 and entropy-rank rho 0.744. The archived report names scikit-learn 1.9 / float32 inputs; this is a same-configuration diagnostic, not an exact numerical reproduction of its 1.3%, 0.66 and 0.76. New raw-vector reruns are EfficientNet-only because the other models' raw vectors are absent here.</p>
<p class=note>Reproduce: <code>python botanical-computer-vision/fieldguidevision-meeting-minimal/soft_audit/run_soft_clustering.py</code>, then <code>python botanical-computer-vision/fieldguidevision-meeting-minimal/soft_audit/update_report.py</code>. Outputs include full responsibility arrays, per-run metrics, example rankings and train component composition. Definitions: <a href='https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.mixture.GaussianMixture.html'>GaussianMixture</a>.</p></dd></dl></section>'''
    s,n=re.subn(r'<section id=e4>.*?</section>',lambda m:section,s,flags=re.S);assert n==1
    s=s.replace('<th>GMM max&lt;0.6</th>','<th>legacy all-fit GMM max&lt;0.6</th>').replace('<th>GMM seed ARI</th>','<th>legacy GMM seed ARI</th>')
    s=re.sub(r'\(5\) Soft GMM membership is near-hard for all three .*?\(6\)',
        '(5) The legacy all-corpus diagonal GMM gave near-hard memberships; this is model-conditional allocation, not evidence against biological overlap. See the corrected train-only uncertainty audit in section 4. (6)',s)
    yolo='''<section id=e10><h2>10. YOLO organ detection / segmentation: proposed comparison</h2><div><span class='b e'>Experiment plan</span> <span class='b x'>Not run: checkpoint and instance labels needed</span></div>
<p><b>Run a paired localization experiment before replacing the whole analysis.</b> For organ detection/segmentation, YOLO changes which pixels reach the downstream encoder. Compare the same images as (A) whole image, (B) predicted organ-box crop and (C) predicted organ mask with fixed background fill, keeping the downstream encoder unchanged. Add ground-truth crops/masks as an upper-bound control on annotated images. This separates localization benefit from encoder changes.</p>
<div class=tw><table><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Measure</th><th>Required control</th></tr>
<tr><td>Detection</td><td>Per-organ precision/recall; box mAP50–95; small-object and missed-image rates</td><td>Human organ boxes; fixed threshold chosen on validation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Instance segmentation</td><td>Mask mAP50–95; matched IoU/Dice; missed instances</td><td>Human instance masks; fixed matching and occlusion policy</td></tr>
<tr><td>Downstream representation</td><td>Organ/species macro-F1; PCA; K sweep; audited soft memberships</td><td>Same encoder, images and individual-plant-disjoint splits for whole/crop/mask inputs</td></tr>
<tr><td>System behavior</td><td>No-detection fallback, multiple-instance aggregation, speed and memory</td><td>Count failures in the denominator; named device/input size</td></tr></table></div>
<p>Every crop from one image and every image of one individual must remain in its original split. Fit transforms and models on train; choose thresholds/checkpoints on validation; reserve test for the final fixed protocol. Multiple-organ ground truth requires real instance/multi-label annotation; single canonical image labels do not generate boxes or masks. A YOLO detection confidence and a GMM membership are different quantities.</p>
<p>No YOLO result is claimed here. The checkout has no supplied organ YOLO checkpoint and no filled organ box/mask ground truth. Standard COCO-pretrained models are a starting point for fine-tuning on a custom organ ontology, not validated recognizers for this label set. The full executable experiment specification is documented in <code>YOLO_EVALUATION_PLAN.md</code>; actual training/inference still requires the exact model/weights, images, annotations and hardware budget.</p>
<p class=note>Official task references: <a href='https://docs.ultralytics.com/tasks/detect/'>YOLO detection</a> · <a href='https://docs.ultralytics.com/tasks/segment/'>YOLO instance segmentation</a>.</p></section>'''
    if '<section id=e10>' in s:
        s,n=re.subn(r'<section id=e10>.*?</section>',lambda m:yolo,s,flags=re.S);assert n==1
    else:
        s=s.replace('<section><h2>Reproduce</h2>',yolo+'<section><h2>Reproduce</h2>')
        s=s.replace('<a href=#e9>K sensitivity</a></nav>','<a href=#e9>K sensitivity</a><a href=#e10>YOLO plan</a></nav>')
    REPORT.write_text(s);print('Replaced soft clustering, labelled legacy appendix metrics, added YOLO comparison plan.')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
